{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaRoXY5vELLJ3FPcuyFm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `plus_eq_add` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof works by induction on `m`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem plus_eq_add (n m : Nat) : plus n m = n + m := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => rfl\n  | succ m ih => simp [plus, ih, Nat.add_assoc]\n```\n\n- **When `m` is 0:** `plus n 0` reduces to `n` by definition, which is the same as `n + 0`, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **When `m` is `m + 1`:** `plus n (m + 1)` unfolds to `plus n m + 1`. The induction hypothesis turns that into `(n + m) + 1`, and `Nat.add_assoc` regroups it to match `n + (m + 1)`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":8298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":283,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf47dc20-c3a8-44e7-a5d6-43b77513e839","uuid":"1790ca7b-494c-473a-8bc8-de58512308ef","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:54:46.459Z","request_id":"req_011CgaRoXFTjUGNVPXBCeRgR"}
